  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Carbon Asset Development Fund (CADF) Multi Donor Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The CPF concept and development objectives were discussed and approved  by the World Bank Board of Directors on September 25, 2007. The CPF is  aimed at promoting demonstration, strategic, and transformational  programmatic Emission Reduction (ER) activities.
 
 The CPF is composed of two trust funds: the Carbon Asset Development  Fund (CADF) and the Carbon Fund.  This TFP is for the Carbon Asset  Development Fund of the CPF.  The CADF provides funding for the  development of ER assets and programs through Bank work and recipient  executed grant support to client work; administrativeand Trustee  services; and to provide technical assistance and capacity building  support.
 
 The second trust fund, the CPF Carbon Fund, will focus on payments for  ER credits from Progams developed by Sellers in the Facility. The CPF  Carbon Fund will have several tranches, and the information on the  CADF presented here is based on an assumption of a Euro 350 million  first tranche of the CPF Carbon Fund only. See separate TFP for the  CPF Carbon Fund for details.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
